 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2019-03-13",
   "text": "Bank on Students Emergency Loan Refinancing Act\n This bill revises requirements concerning student loan debt. \n Specifically, the bill establishes a program that allows eligible individuals with federal or private student loans to refinance them down to the lower rates offered to new federal borrowers in the 2016-2017 school year under certain circumstances. \n In addition, the bill requires an individual taxpayer whose adjusted gross income exceeds $1 million to pay a minimum tax rate of 30% of the excess of the taxpayer's adjusted gross income over the taxpayer's modified charitable contribution deduction for the taxable year (commonly known as the tentative fair share tax)."
  }
 ],
